```
  ═══ DOUBLE-CHECKED LOCKING vs STABLE VALUE ═══

  Double-Checked Locking:
    private volatile X resource;
    if (resource == null) {          ← check 1 (no lock)
        synchronized(this) {         ← lock
            if (resource == null) {   ← check 2 (inside lock)
                resource = new X();
            }
        }
    }
    return resource;
    // 8 lines, volatile required, easy to break

  StableValue:
    private final StableValue<X> resource = StableValue.of();
    return resource.orElseSet(X::new);
    // 2 lines, thread-safe, JVM-optimizable, impossible to break
